SLIDE 2: THE OCEAN PLASTIC CRISIS
Layout: Title + 2 Columns
Slide Title:

text

THE OCEAN PLASTIC CRISIS
A Problem Too Big to Ignore
Left Column - Statistics:

text

🌊 8 MILLION TONS
Plastic entering oceans annually

🇮🇳 7,500 KM
Indian coastline under threat

💰 ₹300 CRORE
Annual cleanup costs

❌ 70% FAILURE RATE
Missed by reactive cleanup

🐢 250+ SPECIES
Endangered marine life at risk

📈 ₹1.5 LAKH CRORE
Fisheries sector threatened
Right Column - The Gap:

text

EXISTING SOLUTIONS FAIL:

❌ Satellite Tracking
   • ₹50+ Lakhs per deployment
   • 48-72 hour data delays
   • 5km resolution (too coarse)
   • Inaccessible to local authorities

❌ Manual Cleanup
   • Reactive, not preventive
   • Labor-intensive
   • Misses 70% of drift plastic
   • High operational costs

❌ Coastal Surveillance
   • Limited range
   • No predictive capability
   • Weather dependent
Bottom Banner:

text

"We're fighting ocean pollution blindfolded. 
It's time to predict, not just react."
Design Recommendations:

Use icons for each statistic (from Flaticon or Icons8)
Red X marks for failed solutions
Before/after images: polluted beach vs clean beach
Use infographic style with bold numbers
Visual Assets:

Top: Polluted beach photo (Getty Images/Unsplash)
Right: Comparison chart showing satellite vs ground truth delay
Background: Subtle wave pattern watermark
Speaker Notes:

text

Every 60 seconds, a garbage truck worth of plastic enters our oceans. 
India's coastline faces ₹300 crore in annual cleanup costs, yet we're 
missing 70% of drifting plastic because current methods are reactive. 
Satellite tracking costs ₹50 lakhs and delivers data too late. Manual 
cleanup crews arrive after ecosystem damage is done. We needed a better way.
