• LoRa/GSM          • Tailwind CSS        • LSTM Networks

Database:           
• MySQL 8.0 / Supabase / MongoDB
Design Recommendations:

Use distinct colors for each layer (Blue→Green→Purple→Orange)
Arrows with animated flow effect
Icons for each technology
Clean, modern flowchart style
Visual Assets:

Layer icons from Font Awesome Pro
Tech stack logos (official brand assets)
Data flow animation (subtle pulse along arrows)
Speaker Notes:

text

Our architecture is built on five layers. Layer 1: IoT sensors measure 
temperature, water quality, and location via Arduino. Layer 2: Node.js 
backend validates and stores data. Layer 3: Python ML engine processes 
environmental parameters through our hybrid LSTM-Physics model to predict 
drift. Layer 4: React dashboard with Three.js renders 3D ocean 
visualizations in real-time. We integrate with INCOIS and NOAA for 
validation data. The entire pipeline processes data in under 200 
milliseconds per prediction.
SLIDE 5: AI & MACHINE LEARNING ENGINE
Layout: Title + Split Screen (Technical Details)
Slide Title:

text

AI PREDICTION ENGINE
Hybrid Machine Learning + Ocean Physics
Left Side - Model Architecture:

text

🧠 HYBRID AI-PHYSICS MODEL

┌────────────────────────────┐
│   INPUT FEATURES (8)       │
├────────────────────────────┤
│ • Sea Surface Temperature  │
│ • Current Velocity (U,V)   │
│ • Wind Speed & Direction   │
│ • Salinity / TDS           │
│ • Plastic Density Class    │
│ • Wave Height              │
└────────────────────────────┘
           ↓
┌────────────────────────────┐
│   LSTM NEURAL NETWORK      │
├────────────────────────────┤
│ • 2 Layers, 64 Units       │
│ • Dropout: 0.3             │
│ • Learns temporal patterns │
└────────────────────────────┘
           ↓
┌────────────────────────────┐
│  PHYSICS CONSTRAINT LAYER  │
├────────────────────────────┤
│ • Lagrangian Drift Eq.     │
│ • Stokes Drift Correction  │
│ • Wind Drag Coefficient    │
└────────────────────────────┘
           ↓
┌────────────────────────────┐
│   OUTPUT (Δ Lat, Δ Lon)    │
│   24-48 Hour Prediction    │
└────────────────────────────┘
