Design Recommendations:

Left: Neural network diagram with animated nodes
Right: Gauge charts for accuracy metrics
Use green checkmarks for dataset items
Include sample heatmap showing prediction vs actual drift
Color code: Purple for AI, Blue for Physics, Green for Output
Visual Assets:

Neural network architecture diagram (create in draw.io)
Accuracy gauge (Chartist.js or similar)
Sample prediction map overlay
Training dataset icons
Speaker Notes:

text

Our AI engine's secret? Hybrid intelligence. We don't just rely on 
black-box machine learning. We combine LSTM neural networks with 
Lagrangian ocean physics equations - the same math that governs real 
particle drift. This fusion reduces training data needs by 60% while 
achieving 85% accuracy. We've trained on 6 years of INCOIS ocean data, 
validated against 15,000 actual cleanup records. The model predicts 
24-hour drift in under 200 milliseconds - fast enough for real-time alerts.
