This isn't just a concept - it's working hardware. Our prototype uses 
commodity components: Arduino Mega, waterproof DS18B20 sensors, TDS 
meters, and GPS - all integrated in an IP67 enclosure. We've completed 
120+ hours of continuous field testing with 5 nodes achieving 99.2% 
uptime. The total cost? ₹48,500 per node versus ₹50 lakh satellite 
systems. We're at TRL 6 - ready for pilot deployment. Next quarter, 
we're deploying 20 nodes off Rameswaram coast.
